    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0325" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/618: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-22T16:00:00+09:00">April 22, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 23—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. Department’s 96, April 16, 1 p.m. and 103, April 20, 5 p.m., traffic of the
                    Yangtze, et cetera. Emphatic representations were made to the Foreign Office
                    yesterday covering all of the points in the telegrams under reference. Mail copy
                    of our note and memorandum of conversation going forward pouch April 27.<anchor
                        n="54" xml:id="d373-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
